.SH "ARRAYS AND ASSOCIATIVE ARRAYS"
.B typeset -a arr
declares a normal array;
.B typeset -A assoc
declares an associative array. Arrays are 1-indexed by default; set
.B KSH_ARRAYS
for 0-indexed semantics.
.PP
.B Element ops:
.BR ${arr[i]} ", " ${arr[-1]} " (last), " ${arr[1,3]} " (slice),"
.BR ${#arr} " (length), " ${arr[@]} " (all)."
.PP
.B Assoc ops:
.BR ${assoc[key]} ", " ${(k)assoc} " (keys), " ${(v)assoc} " (values),"
.BR ${(kv)assoc} " (interleaved)."
.PP
.B Append:
.B arr+=(elt)
\(em append element;
.B "arr[i]+=text"
\(em concat to element;
.B assoc+=(k v)
\(em add key.
.SH "ARITHMETIC"
.B (( expr ))
returns 0 if
.I expr
is non-zero, 1 otherwise.
.B $((expr))
substitutes the result. Operators (highest precedence first):
.PP
.RS
.B "** "
(exponent)
.br
.B "! ~ - +"
(unary)
.br
.B "* / %"
.br
.B "+ -"
.br
.B "<< >>"
.br
.B "< <= > >="
.br
.B "== !="
.br
.B "&  ^  |"
.br
.B "&&  ||"
.br
.B "?:"
(ternary)
.br
.B "= += -= *= /= %= **= <<= >>= &= ^= |=  &&= ||="
.RE
.PP
Float support requires
.B typeset -F
or
.BR "typeset -E ."
Math functions
.RB ( sin ", " cos ", " sqrt ", " exp ", " log ", " atan ", " ceil ", " floor ", " ...)
load via
.BR "zmodload zsh/mathfunc" .
.SH "CONDITIONAL EXPRESSIONS"
.B [[ expr ]]
returns 0 (true) or 1 (false). Word splitting and filename generation
do not apply inside; the right-hand side of pattern operators is a
glob (or regex for
.BR =~ ).
.SS "File tests"
.TP
.B -a
file exists.
.TP
.B -b
block special.
.TP
.B -c
character special.
.TP
.B -d
directory.
.TP
.B -e
exists.
.TP
.B -f
regular file.
.TP
.B -g
setgid.
.TP
.B -h " / " -L
symbolic link.
.TP
.B -k
sticky bit.
.TP
.B -p
named pipe.
.TP
.B -r " / " -w " / " -x
readable / writable / executable.
.TP
.B -s
non-zero size.
.TP
.B -u
setuid.
.TP
.B -O " / " -G
owned by EUID / EGID.
.TP
.B -N
mtime newer than atime.
.TP
.B -S
socket.
.SS "Binary file tests"
.B file1 -nt file2
(newer),
.B -ot
(older),
.B -ef
(same dev+inode).
.SS "String tests"
.B -n s
non-empty;
.B -z s
empty;
.B s == pat
glob match;
.B s != pat
glob mismatch;
.B s =~ regex
ERE match (sets
.BR $MATCH ", " $match ", " $BASH_REMATCH );
.B s1 < s2
lex less;
.B s1 > s2
greater.
.SS "Numeric tests"
.B -eq -ne -lt -le -gt -ge .
.SS "Boolean composition"
.B "!"
.B "&&"
.B "||"
with operator precedence; parenthesise with
.BR "( ... )" .
.SH "GLOB PATTERNS"
.SS "Basic"
.B *
zero or more chars.
.B ?
exactly one char.
.B [chars]
class.
.B [!chars]
negation.
.B [a-z]
range.
.B [[:alpha:]]
POSIX classes
.RB ( alpha ", " alnum ", " digit ", " upper ", " lower ", " space ", " punct ", " cntrl ", " print ", " graph ", " xdigit ", " blank ).
.SS "Extended (EXTENDED_GLOB)"
.B **/
recursive match (across directories).
.B ***/
like
.B **/
but follows symlinks.
.B (foo|bar)
alternation.
.B ^pat
exclude pattern.
.B pat~excl
match
.I pat
except
.IR excl .
.B <NUM-NUM>
numeric range (
.BR <-> " any number, " "<0-99>" " 0\(en99)."
.B #
zero or more of preceding atom (like
.BR * );
.B ##
one or more.
.SS "Glob qualifiers"
.B file*(qual)
applies file-system filters. Common qualifiers:
.TP
.B /
directories only.
.TP
.B .
plain files only.
.TP
.B @
symlinks only.
.TP
.B = " / " p " / " *
sockets / pipes / executables.
.TP
.B r,w,x
readable / writable / executable by user;
.BR R , W , X
by anyone;
.BR A , I , E
group / other.
.TP
.B u\fIuser\fR " / " g\fIgroup\fR
owned by
.IR user " / " group .
.TP
.B L\fI[+-]n[kmgptKMGPT]\fR
size match (k/m/g/p/t suffixes; +/- for greater/lesser).
.TP
.B s, S, t, T
size in bytes / blocks / lines.
.TP
.BR m [mhdwM] [+-]n
modified within / after / before
.I n
minutes / hours / days / weeks / months.
.TP
.BR a [mhdwM] [+-]n
accessed within;
.BR c [mhdwM]
ctime.
.TP
.B U, G
owned by current UID / GID.
.TP
.B oc, on, oN, oL, om, oa, od
sort by ctime / name / Name / size / mtime / atime / dirname.
.B O
inverts (descending).
.TP
.B [n,m]
slice the result list.
.TP
.B D
include dotfiles.
.TP
.B N
NULL_GLOB: empty result is OK, no error.
.TP
.B -
follow symlinks for tests.
.TP
.B e:\fIcode\fR:
arbitrary shell test; the file passes if
.I code
returns true.
.PP
Qualifiers chain:
.B *(.Lk+10om[1,5])
\(em plain files larger than 10K, oldest 5 by mtime.
.SH "JOB CONTROL"
.B MONITOR
on for interactive shells. Suffix
.B &
to background.
.B Ctrl-Z
suspends.
.B fg %N
foregrounds job
.IR N ;
.B bg %N
resumes in background.
.B jobs
lists;
.B disown %N
detaches from the shell;
.B kill %N
signals a job; named jobs by
.B %%
(current),
.BR %+ ,
.BR %- ,
or
.BI %? str
(match by command substring).
.B NOTIFY
prints state changes immediately;
.B no_notify
defers to next prompt.
.SH "FUNCTIONS"
.B function name {body}
or
.B name () {body}
defines a function. Local variables: prefix with
.BR local ,
.BR typeset ,
.BR declare ,
.BR integer ,
.BR float ,
.BR private .
Functions inherit
.BR $1 ... $N
positional args; the calling positional set is restored on return.
.PP
.B autoload \-Uz fnname
defers loading until first call; the function body is read from a
file named
.I fnname
along
.BR $fpath .
.B \-U
disables alias expansion at load time.
.B \-z
forces zsh-style parsing.
.PP
.B Special hook names:
.B preexec
(before each command),
.B precmd
(before each prompt),
.B chpwd
(after cd),
.B zshexit
(on shell exit),
.B periodic
(every
.B $PERIOD
seconds),
.BR TRAPDEBUG / TRAPERR / TRAPEXIT
(trap handlers).
.B zle-line-init
.B zle-line-pre-redraw
.B zle-line-finish
.B zle-keymap-select
.B zle-isearch-update
.B zle-isearch-exit
are ZLE hooks.
.SH "BUILTINS"
The full upstream set is implemented; below groups them by category.
For per-option detail see
.BR zshbuiltins (1).
.PP
.B Flow control:
.BR break ,
.BR continue ,
.BR return ,
.BR exit ,
.BR true ,
.BR false ,
.BR : .
.PP
.B Variable mgmt:
.BR typeset ,
.BR declare ,
.BR local ,
.BR private ,
.BR readonly ,
.BR export ,
.BR float ,
.BR integer ,
.BR unset ,
