.SH "DAEMON COORDINATION"
When run in full mode (no parity flag), zshrs cooperates with a
singleton coordinator process,
.BR zshrs-daemon ,
addressed via
.IR ~/.cache/zshrs/daemon.sock .
The daemon owns ALL mutation:
.IP \fBfsnotify\fR 8
watches
.IR ~/.zshrc ,
.BR $fpath ,
plugin trees; invalidates affected cache shards on change.
.IP \fBcompile\fR 8
rkyv image writes for script_cache, plugin_cache, autoload_cache,
catalog.db rebuilds, log rotation, integrity scans.
.IP "\fBIPC routing\fR" 8
cross-shell pub/sub
.RB ( zsubscribe ,
.BR znotify ,
.BR zsend ,
.BR ztag ),
shell registry
.RB ( zls ,
.BR zid ,
.BR zping ),
and the session-persistent job supervisor
.RB ( zjob ,
planned).
.PP
100+ thin
.B zshrs
clients (e.g. one per tmux pane) mmap the daemon's outputs directly
for hot lookups (zero IPC) and use the socket only for control-plane
events (rebuild, fpath_changed, stats_flush, cross-shell dispatch).
Clients spawn zero background threads, polling timers, or SQLite
handles. See
.BR zd (1)
for daemon administration.
.PP
.B POSIX mode never spawns the daemon.
.SH "AHEAD-OF-TIME COMPILATION"
.B \-\-aot
.RI ( script.zsh )
emits a single self-contained executable that bundles
.B fusevm
with the script's compiled bytecode. The result has zero runtime
dependency on the
.B zshrs
binary and can be distributed as a standalone artifact. AOT and the
daily-driver cache are two separate tracks: AOT for deploy binaries;
the rkyv cache for the interactive shell.
.SH "ASPECT-ORIENTED INTERCEPTS"
.B zshrs
supports
.BR before ,
.BR after ,
and
.B around
advice on every command, builtin, and user function. Advice is
registered via the
.B intercepts
crate (see
.IR src/intercepts/ )
and runs in-process inside fusevm \(em no
.BR fork (2)
\(em which makes it cheap enough for production tracing, profiling,
auditing, or per-command behaviour overlays. This is the foundation
for
.BR zpwrTrace ,
.BR zpwrFlame ,
.B zpwrTop
and the rest of the
.B zpwr
introspection stack.
.SH "WORKERS & NO-FORK ARCHITECTURE"
zshrs ships a persistent worker pool: long-lived processes that
service builtins, common externals
.RB ( ls ", " cat ", " grep ", "
etc., on the user's allowlist), and pipeline stages without invoking
.BR fork (2)
on every command. This is invisible to scripts: pipelines compose,
redirections work, job control behaves identically. Workers can be
disabled via
.B "setopt no_workers"
or by the parity flags.
.SH "RECORDER"
.B zshrs-recorder
.RI ( bins/zshrs-recorder.rs )
captures shell sessions as a structured event stream. Feature-gated;
see
.BR docs/RECORDER.md " and " docs/RECORDER_PROTOCOL.md
for the on-disk schema. The replay surface
.RB ( zpwrReplay )
sits on top of it.
.SH "ENVIRONMENT"
Standard zsh-recognised variables (see SPECIAL PARAMETERS) plus
zshrs additions:
.TP
.B ZSHRS_CACHE
Override the cache root. Default:
.IR ~/.cache/zshrs/ .
.TP
.B ZSHRS_LOG
.BR tracing -style filter for the structured log. Examples:
.BR debug ", " "zshrs::ported::lex=trace" ", " "zshrs=info,fusevm=trace" .
.TP
.B ZSHRS_LONG_CMD_PRE_THRESHOLD
Seconds. Commands taking longer fire the preexec long-cmd hook.
.TP
.B ZSHRS_NO_DAEMON
Suppress daemon connection (per-invocation override of full mode).
.SH "FILES"
.TP
.I ~/.cache/zshrs/
Cache root. Sharded as
.IB {hash8} - {slug} .rkyv
per source root, plus
.BR catalog.db ,
.BR daemon.sock ,
.BR zshrs.log .
.TP
.I ~/.config/zshrs/zshrs-daemon.toml
Optional daemon config; see
.BR zd (1).
.TP
.I ~/.zshenv,\ ~/.zprofile,\ ~/.zshrc,\ ~/.zlogin,\ ~/.zlogout
Standard zsh startup files (used identically to upstream zsh).
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
Identical to
.BR zsh (1):
the shell exits with the status of the last command or with
.B $?
at the time of an
.B exit
call. 127 indicates command-not-found; 126 indicates a permission
error. Trap handlers and
.B zshexit
fire before the actual exit syscall.
.SH "COMPATIBILITY GUARANTEES"
.B zshrs
treats the zsh upstream
.B C
source under
.IR src/zsh/Src/
as the spec floor. Bytecode and SQLite formats are versioned and
migration-safe; old caches either upgrade cleanly or rebuild
silently. A
.IR .zshrc " " "that worked yesterday"
must work today. Compat-floor regressions against
.BR zpwr ,
.BR zsh-more-completions ,
.BR oh-my-zsh ,
.BR zinit ,
.BR p10k ,
and the standard plugin set are catastrophic; the parity test corpus
.RB ( tests/zsh_compat_parity_gaps.rs ,
20,000+ cases) is gating.
.PP
.B Architectural invariants:
.IP "" 4
.B tree_walker_absent
\(em the C-style AST walker is unreachable from any code path.
fusevm bytecode is the only executor.
.IP "" 4
.B no_tree_walker_dispatch
\(em no Rust call-site re-introduces an
.BR execlist / execpline / execcmd
shape; pinned at 96 tests.
.IP "" 4
.B port_purity
\(em every
.B pub fn
under
.B src/ported/
maps to a real
.B Src/x.c
function name (allowlist in
.BR tests/data/fake_fn_allowlist.txt ).
.IP "" 4
.B file_mapping
\(em ports live in the Rust file matching their C basename
(allowlist in
.BR tests/data/ported_fn_file_mapping_allowlist.txt ).
.SH "DIAGNOSTICS"
Errors take the form
.BI "zshrs: " command ": " reason
on stderr. Informational chatter (init, indexing, autoload pre-warm,
plugin compile) goes to
.IR ~/.cache/zshrs/zshrs.log
via
.BR tracing ;
it is never printed to the terminal. No startup banner. No deprecation
nags. No spell-correction prompts. No "did you mean" hints. No
tip-of-the-day. No "use \fB\-\-help\fR for more" suffix in error
messages.
.SH "DEBUGGING & INTROSPECTION"
.TP
.B \-\-disasm
Print fusevm opcodes before VM execution.
.TP
.B \-\-dump\-tokens
Token stream from lex.rs.
.TP
.B \-\-dump\-ast
Parsed AST from parse.rs.
.TP
.B \-\-dump\-wordcode
zsh-style wordcode (for parity comparison against
.BR zcompile ).
.TP
.B \-\-dump\-zwc
Inspect a
.B *.zwc
bytecode bundle.
.TP
.B \-\-doctor
Full diagnostic report; useful when filing issues.
.TP
.B ZSHRS_LOG
.BR tracing -style filter on the structured log.
